xnu 0115: give the sampler a clock the board delivers and a screen heartbeat

The sampler thread's tsleep() timeout never fires on this board, so the only
samples that used to arrive came from the UFS write path, and 0113 removed
that call: the 0114 run logged one sample and then nothing, which leaves a
stalled boot and a slow one impossible to tell apart.

The framebuffer's vsync timer does run (60 Hz, re-armed by its own callback),
so tick the sampler from it every five seconds. Also move a white block on the
panel twice a second, written straight into the framebuffer: the panel scans
that memory by itself, so when the console goes quiet the block still says
whether the kernel runs or is wedged. It stops at the first swap, when the UI
takes the screen.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/MondrianFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -293,6 +293,33 @@
 	}
 	IOLockUnlock(fb->fLock);
 	sender->setTimeoutUS(MONDRIAN_FB_VSYNC_US);
+	/*
+	 * The kernel's tsleep() timeouts never fire on this board, so the
+	 * sampler's own thread ticks once and sleeps for ever. This timer does
+	 * run: give the sampler a clock it can trust, every five seconds.
+	 */
+	if ((count % (MONDRIAN_FB_REFRESH_HZ * 5)) == 0) {
+		extern "C" void mondrian_sample_tick(void);
+		mondrian_sample_tick();
+	}
+	/*
+	 * Liveness marker that needs neither the console nor printf: the panel
+	 * scans this memory by itself, so a block that moves twice a second
+	 * proves the kernel still runs when the log has stopped. It goes away
+	 * with the console at the first swap, when the UI owns the screen.
+	 */
+	if (!fb->fConsolePaused && (count % (MONDRIAN_FB_REFRESH_HZ / 2)) == 0) {
+		uint32_t phase = (uint32_t)((count / (MONDRIAN_FB_REFRESH_HZ / 2)) & 1);
+		uint8_t *row = (uint8_t *)fb->fPixels + (size_t)(phase ? 72 : 16) * fb->fRowBytes;
+
+		for (uint32_t y = 0; y < 32; y++) {
+			uint32_t *pixel = (uint32_t *)(row + (size_t)y * fb->fRowBytes) + 16;
+
+			for (uint32_t x = 0; x < 64; x++) {
+				pixel[x] = 0x00ffffff;
+			}
+		}
+	}
 }
 
 void
